      "completion_note": "NFR-2 measurement, taken 2026-08-20 on this repository (57 source files, 34894 production lines, 57097 physical .rs lines, above the 50k floor), Clippy-only plan with every rust_doctor::* rule off, release binaries of 90956b1 (no walk) and of this epic (walk), sharing one CARGO_TARGET_DIR. Cold Clippy cache: 4.467 s without the walk, 4.487 s with it. Warm Clippy cache, median of three runs after a warm-up: 0.106 s without, 0.205 s with. The walk therefore costs about 0.098 s of wall clock, which is 2.2 % of a scan that actually compiles and stays under the 15 % bound for any scan longer than about 0.65 s. It exceeds the bound only on a re-scan whose Clippy cache is fully warm, where Clippy compiles nothing and the whole scan is 0.2 s."
